---
title: Latent
description: Latent is a non-destructive RAW photo editor for the desktop — cull a shoot, develop the keepers, and mask locally, with the original files left untouched.
---

Latent is a desktop RAW editor. You point it at a folder of files, cull the shoot down to the
frames worth keeping, and develop those from the sensor data rather than from a baked JPEG.
Nothing you do rewrites the original: every adjustment lives in a sidecar beside the file.

It is free and open source, and it runs entirely on your machine — no account, no upload, no
catalogue service in the middle.

## What's in these docs

- [Install](/docs/latent/install) — get the AppImage running.
- [Library & culling](/docs/latent/library) — folders, collections, ratings, picks and rejects.
- [Develop](/docs/latent/develop) — the Light, Curve, Color, Effects, Detail, Optics and Geometry panels.
- [Masks & layers](/docs/latent/masks) — radial, gradient and brush layers, and the adjustments they carry.
- [Presets & history](/docs/latent/presets) — the preset library, saving your own, and stepping back.
- [Files & sidecars](/docs/latent/files) — what Latent writes to disk and what it never touches.

## How it relates to NeoWorks

Latent is a local tool and stands on its own — it does not need a NeoWorks account to run. What
it does not do is store anything for you. If you want the results backed up and synced across
devices, that is what a NeoWorks plan and its encrypted
[storage](/docs/neoworks/encryption) are for; the platform holds ciphertext it cannot read.
